I fixed both halves of #1106 and committed it as ec24eaf0. fmt, clippy (-D warnings), build and the full cargo test all pass.

What changed in `src/memory.rs`:
• (a) The store no longer freezes. When it already holds 20 auto entries, auto_remember_to now drops the oldest auto entry and saves the new one. Before, it refused every new note forever. /remember entries are never dropped and don't count toward the 20. The memory full … use /forget warning is gone; when an old entry is replaced, the save line says "(replaced the oldest auto-saved memory)".
• Marking auto entries. Entries now carry an auto field. It defaults to false and isn't written to the file when false, so files holding only /remember entries look exactly as before.
• Old stores un-freeze too. Entries saved before this field existed load as auto: false, which would leave a full old store frozen. So an entry also counts as auto if it starts with the exact text the two note builders write (Watch fix: ', or one of the [build] … / [bug] Test expectation prefixes followed by  in  ). The builder and this check read one shared prefix table, so they can't drift apart. The cost is in the doc comment and commit: a /remember` note typed to start with one of those exact openings would count as auto.
• (b) Empty panic headers aren't saved. A test failure whose message is only thread 'x' panicked at file:line:col: with nothing after it is skipped. When the assertion text is present, the note now puts it first (cut to 120 characters on a character boundary), then the test name and location. Before, a long test name used up the 120 characters and cut the assertion off. Old-style panic messages and plain assertion text are saved as before.
• (c) not needed: the commit explains why. The store is bounded at 20 auto entries and they are now the newest, so a separate cap on what reaches the prompt adds nothing.

Tests:
• There are 10 new tests in src/memory_evict_tests.rs. They cover saving under the cap (same result as before), eviction at the cap, /remember entries surviving a full store, an old frozen store un-freezing, near-miss notes that only resemble the builder prefixes, and the panic-header cases.
• The old test_auto_remember_refuses_when_full asserted the bug itself. I inverted it and renamed it test_auto_remember_evicts_oldest_when_full.
• The #672 dedup tests are untouched and still pass.
• I checked that the new tests can actually fail. Breaking the old-store recognition made the two old-store tests fail by name. Breaking the empty-header check made the content-free test fail. I restored the code after each check and confirmed nothing broken was left behind.

Docs: docs/src/usage/commands.md now explains automatic memories: the 20 newest are kept, /remember entries are never removed automatically, and bare panic headers aren't saved. ARCHITECTURE.md has a new memory.rs entry. memory.rs is 1975 lines, under the 2000-line limit.

I didn't edit this repo's .yoyo/memory.json. It should fix itself as new notes replace the old ones, but I haven't seen that happen in a real run yet. Every #1106 mention in the code is a past-tense comment, so nothing user-facing will point at a closed ticket once the push closes it.
